  "summary": "Enamel-on-masonite jungle fantasia: koh? — saturated birds, elephants and fish from one Dar es Salaam school.",
  "description": "Tingatinga began with Edward Saidi Tingatinga's 1968 experiments: house paint on ceiling board? — masonite squares, painting buffalo, peacocks and leopards in saturated, almost psychedelic color that sold to expats within hours. After his 1972 death, relatives and students formalized the Tingatinga Arts Cooperative Society, adding dense pattern-fish, dancing birds and baobabs to a shared grammar: flat perspective, dark outlines, compressed jungle abundance. Tourist markets spread it across East Africa and the globe as Tanzania's signature popular art.",
